(3885, 'nimiq4', 'If you are new to ESP32 CAM getting started needs some extra info. not provided by the seller.The chip has no ID so when you try to use Arduino IDE you\'ll need this:- select board \"AI Thinker ESP32-CAM\"- find and load sketch CameraWebServer (I downloaded from internet).- In the sketch select the #define CAMERA_MODEL_AI_THINKER, remark out other options.- Add your ssid and pwd.- Now upload to the ESP32.- open Tools Serial monitor in IDE to get IP address.Board does work....eventually!', '2023-12-27 14:43:04', 'Positive', '154458099177', 'ESP32 CAM Development Board WIFI Blutetooth Camera Power Interface with Antenna', '9.49', '2199498414012', '2426011226005', '154458099177-2426011226005', '2024-01-10 09:05:32', NULL),
