(4315, 'joh.sjo.v8o1rtivta', 'My \"due diligence\" research after I\'d ordered with the LR2032 option, revealed the limitations & dangers of its primitive  200 ohm charge current limiter (over-volt the LR cell, wearing it out in rather short order or cause a CR2032 to explode when powered of a 5 volt rail (3.3v would be safe for the LR cell because it wouldn\'t be enough to even charge it!). I removed that resistor only AFTER I\'d tested it. Ignore the LR option & fit a CR2032 before removing the resistor only after it tests ok', '2024-02-03 19:15:53', 'Positive', '155491320233', 'RTC DS1302 DS1307 DS3231 PCF8563 AT24C32 IIC Real Time Clock for Arduino PI UK', '4.99', '2209082889012', '2435075412005', '155491320233-2435075412005', '2024-02-04 22:40:25', NULL),
